<small>A Song of degrees.</small><br /><sup><b>1</b></sup> In my distress I cried unto the LORD, and he heard me.<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> Deliver my soul, O LORD, from lying lips, <i>and</i> from a deceitful tongue.<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> What shall be given unto thee? or what shall be done unto thee, thou false tongue?<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> Sharp arrows of the mighty, with coals of juniper.<br />
<sup><b>5</b></sup> Woe is me, that I sojourn in Mesech, <i>that</i> I dwell in the tents of Kedar!<br />
<sup><b>6</b></sup> My soul hath long dwelt with him that hateth peace.<br />
<sup><b>7</b></sup> I <i>am for</i> peace: but when I speak, they <i>are</i> for war. <br />
